FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus factor: whose code is still here

I used `git blame` (surviving lines) instead of commit counts. I ignored the formatting commit `62628c0`, which would otherwise have given Fiona Formatter 291 lines. I also used `-w -M -C` so whitespace changes and moved lines count for the original author. Scope: 7 JS files, 1,202 lines.

**Project bus factor: 1.** Troy Goode alone owns 56% of surviving lines. Troy and Douglas Christopher Wilson together own 89%.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Commits (all history) | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 676 | 56% | 95 | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 394 | 33% | 143 | 2021-09-07 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 | 2.5% | 4 | 2015-05-28 |
| Eric di Domenico | 16 | 1.3% | 3 | 2013-10-05 |
| Alberto Leal | 15 | 1.2% | 2 | 2014-05-12 |
| About 25 others | 71 | 5.9% | | |

**Commit counts point to the wrong person.** Douglas has the most commits (143), but Troy owns more of the code that survives.

### Per file

| File | Lines | Top owner | Share | Authors |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the only source file) | 238 | Troy Goode | 66% | 19 |
| `test/test.js` | 731 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 46% | 13 |
| `test/example-app.js` | 81 | Troy Goode | 82% | 2 |
| `test/error-response.js` | 66 | Troy Goode | 86% | 2 |
| `test/issue-2.js` | 48 | Troy Goode | 83% | 2 |
| `test/vary.js` | 36 | Troy Goode | 100% | 1 |
| `test/support/env.js` | 2 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 100% | 1 |

### Risks

- **Troy is the main owner of the library itself.** He owns 66% of `lib/index.js`. The other 18 authors share the remaining 34%, so no single one has much of it.
- **Douglas is inactive.** His last commit is from 2021, and he owns 46% of `test/test.js`. Roughly half of the largest test file has no recent maintainer.
- **The whole repo looks dormant.** There are no commits in the last 90 days. The newest commit is the 2026-04-12 reformat, and Troy's last real commit is 2026-04-10. That is about 6 months ago, so he may be inactive too.
- **`test/vary.js` has a single author.** It is small (36 lines), so the risk is low.

### Caveats

- Blame cannot tell who understands the code today. It only shows who wrote the surviving lines.
- Author names are not merged. "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" and "alex94puchades" may be the same person, and so may other aliases. That would slightly raise a few small shares but would not change the top two.
- The importance cross-reference had little to do. `lib/index.js` is the only source file, so every dependency runs through it.

### Recommendations

1. Treat `lib/index.js` as the critical file. Get a second person to review it who isn't Troy.
2. Find an active reviewer for the parts of `test/test.js` that Douglas wrote.
3. Check whether Troy is still reachable. If he isn't, the project's real bus factor is 0.

I can also run blame with `--since` to see who owns the code written in the last year or two, or merge the author aliases if you want that.

